issue_context.body:
I'm trying the [stm32_temp](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/drivers/adc/adc_stm32.c) driver on my G0B1RE custom board.

<img width="500" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1563974/149132178-bcdf84d8-68ea-4be5-a605-9e412f9daffc.png">

This is the characteristics from G0B1 datasheet:
<img width="650" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1563974/149131327-2c8e91e7-b2c1-4a34-86f5-da458fffeb1e.png">

My devicetree looks like this
```
/ {
	model = "GTSB IVM21";
	compatible = "gtsb,ivm21";

	chosen {
		zephyr,console = &usart2;
		zephyr,shell-uart = &usart2;
		zephyr,uart-mcumgr = &usart2;
		zephyr,sram = &sram0;
		zephyr,flash = &flash0;
		zephyr,code-partition = &slot0_partition;
	};
...
	vmain {
		compatible = "voltage-divider";
		io-channels = <&adc1 0>;
		output-ohms = <51000>;
		full-ohms = <(51000 + 51000)>;
	};

	stm-temp {
		label = "DIE_TEMP";
		compatible = "st,stm32-temp";
		io-channels = <&adc1 12>;
		avgslope = <25>;
		v25 = <760>;
		status = "okay";
	};
};
...
&adc1 {
	pinctrl-0 = <&adc1_in0_pa0 &adc1_in1_pa1 &adc1_in2_pa2 &adc1_in3_pa3>;
	status = "okay";
};
```

And I added these into my defconfig
```
CONFIG_SENSOR=y
CONFIG_STM32_TEMP=y
```

with no other changes to my existing application, apart from the devicetree & Kconfig changes, I found that my application fails to read the battery voltage, the channel setup fails here everytime:

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1563974/149129863-deb8b8bb-95e0-4b74-b010-156c7006ad63.png)

I then changed the stm32_temp driver [init](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/drivers/sensor/stm32_temp/stm32_temp.c#L104) to: (I'm not sure what am I doing, just trial and error)

```c
	*accp = (struct adc_channel_cfg){
		.gain = ADC_GAIN_1,
		.reference = ADC_REF_INTERNAL,
		.acquisition_time = ADC_ACQ_TIME_DEFAULT,
		.channel_id = data->channel,
		.differential = 0
	};
```

Then, my application is able to read the ADC properly.

After that, I copied the stm32_temp sample code to my main() and found that the code stuck in the [calibration step](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/drivers/adc/adc_stm32.c#L342), I then edited the stm32_temp driver so that the [calibration is set to false](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/drivers/sensor/stm32_temp/stm32_temp.c#L116).

```c
	*asp = (struct adc_sequence){
		.channels = BIT(data->channel),
		.buffer = &data->sample_buffer,
		.buffer_size = sizeof(data->sample_buffer),
		.resolution = 12,
		.calibrate = false,
	};
```

And now I'm able to read something, but it clearly doesn't work:
```
Current temperature: -172.-199996 °C
Current temperature: -172.-199996 °C
Current temperature: -171.-800003 °C
Current temperature: -171.-800003 °C
```

I'm not sure if it has negative temperature coefficient, this is what I get if I enabled `ntc`:
```
Current temperature: 221.399993 °C
Current temperature: 222.199996 °C
Current temperature: 221.399993 °C
Current temperature: 222.199996 °C
```

I do know that the formula in stm32_temp isn't suppose to "just works", as it uses v25, and I think I need v30 (so probably need to change this [line](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/drivers/sensor/stm32_temp/stm32_temp.c#L76) to += 30?)

I'm on Zephyr 2.7.0 RC3, `CONFIG_PM` is enabled.

[15. ADC.pdf](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/files/7854188/15.ADC.pdf)
[stm32g0b1re.pdf](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/files/7854195/stm32g0b1re.pdf)

